Z||000009||Archie||12-14-2000||07:41 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>I almost never see ANY V8 owners post Qtr. mile times.  Personally I think they are afraid to go that rough on the car (esp. tranny), but thats just my opinion...<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Kinda adds to the mystic of owning a V-8 car, when you know you don't have to get on here and beat your chest about it.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>Besides most of my customers (including me) won't post times without putting up copies of time slips too.<P>I've seen a lot of threads about 1/4 times but IMHO, anyone who brags about times and doesn't have time slips to prove it is a bench racer. Those of us with little or no TimeSlips either have a hard time getting off on weekends or are too old/slow to care. <P>Hey Phil, it depends on what "basic" means. If the "basic" SBC you are talking about is say a 1983 TBI 305 Taxi Cab engine...... then yeah, maybe you've finally found something to brag about. Keep that thought.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Archie<p>[This message has been edited by Archie (edited 12-14-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000010||Phil||12-14-2000||08:21 AM||||Archie:<BR>That's why I said BASIC    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  A turn on a chasis dyno gave me 222 rwhp and 273 ft-lbs. That was right up there and slightly above  a whole bunch on 327's and 350's ("slightly" modified). I know you can build up a 500+ hp SBC but how many really do for a daily driver? I may be a touch bias but I really like my car and really that's all that counts. Playing with Fiero is all just good natured fun. Also people that know my wierd sense of humor are aware that just out of spite I would rather give a good dig instead of a compliment. Must be part of being a plastic death trap owner. See ya in Daytona. BTW to show everyone how libral I am I did install a nitrous mouse motor in my Fiero<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mousemotor_2.jpg"> <P><p>[This message has been edited by Phil (edited 12-14-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||Slammed Fiero||12-14-2000||02:32 PM||||Chris moores 1 northstar car ran 13.6 in the 1/4 before tuning by lingenfelter . No idea what it will run after there done with it. IMHO John norman is full of it 11's before the bottle ,in the hot rod magazine , then goes on to quote it has been put on a dyno and yielded 260 Rear wheel Hp .. I don't think so Skippy. I think high 12's low 13's are what a N* is capable of.<P>Look at the facts ..<BR>290ft lbs of Torque <BR>300hp , more in a fiero with the loss of the powersteering and a free flow exhaust.<BR>the WEIGHT!! ..the N* tranny is a TANK!!. <BR>the car weighs 3100lbs (chris moores car)<P>It doesn't add up . Perhaps a Northstar in a Lotus super 7 will run low 11's , but not a fiero. In the Northstars defense..it's hi tech , smoooooth as silk and gets great milage..while being faster than most any production car.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...||||reg||1
Z||000012||BBBAD GT||12-14-2000||05:31 PM||||I'm with Dan and Slammed, 260 rwhp isn't going to get you in the 11's, not over 2700lb.  I'd say for a street car with street suspension, you would have to be doing min of 114-116 mph to get into the 11's, and thats with good traction.  <P>Haven't taken the V8 to the track yet, mainly because I just got it.  I really don't have much of a need to see what it does, I have the Stang to cure all my face smearing needs.  <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif">     <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A><p>[This message has been edited by BBBAD GT (edited 12-14-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||Wannabe||12-16-2000||05:24 PM||||The case for the SBC is very strong. Anybody see the build up of the 383 sbc the current issue of Hot Rod magazine? They built a mild 383 for under $2000. The engine put out peak torqe of 448 lb-ft and peak hp of 421. Torque output was over 400lb-ft from 2800rpm right through 5500 rpm. That's Viper territory. The article claims the engine will put a Nova or Camaro into the 12's, so a Fiero, assuming the tranny holds, would be close to if not into the 11's. I read this stuff and have a hard time sying no to dropping a SBC into my Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Shaun41178||12-17-2000||02:26 PM||||John norman is not full of it with his elapsed times.  John nhas run a 12.6 with a 275 hp engine version of his car according GM High TEch Performance magazine.  Now he has a 300 hp version in it.  Hot Rod is lying about john running 11's without nitrous.  The 11 second run was with nitrous.  Hot Rod got there info wrong somewhere.  I talked to a freind of John Normans who told me about this.  The 260 rear wheel hp was without nitrous.  According to hot Rod he has his nitrous kit jetted to 120 extra hp and about as much torque too.  With nitrous he has to easily be pushing 350 hp in a Fiero which will make it really haul some butt.  I have dynoed 170 at the wheels and have run a 14.2.  Even without nitrous johns car will move.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Preferred Performance</A>||||reg||1
